\b Architecture snapshot (current state)\b0\par
- \b Gate engine (pure)\b0: \i gate_engine(fd, CONFIG)\i0 composes packs (uses real pack producers if present; otherwise ICU + BGA fallbacks).\par
- \b Gate-pack merger\b0: \i merge_gatepacks(...)\i0 with TTL=\b max\b0, order-preserving gate de-dup, priority=max, last non-empty next\_action.\par
- \b HL7 (single path)\b0: \i parse_hl7_all\i0 normalizes to canonical keys consumed downstream. Legacy \i parse_hl7_labs\i0 optional.\par
- \b Phase-2 calculators split\b0:\par
  \tab \b Calc utils\b0: \i _pick, _bool, _safe_round\i0.\par
  \tab \b Calcs A\b0: qSOFA, MEWS, HEART, GRACE\_coarse, SOFA\_min, SIRS, Sepsis3.\par
  \tab \b Calcs B\b0: Wells-PE/DVT, PERC, PESI/sPESI, MARBURG, GBS, Child-Pugh, corrected\_calcium, anion\_gap, assess\_d\_dimer, assess\_troponin\_delta.\par
- \b Phase-2 bundle (split)\b0:\par
  \tab B1 \i build_labs_norm\i0 (map canonical HL7 to calculator-friendly names; presence-guarded).\par
  \tab B2 \i compute_phase2_scores\i0 (pure; returns structured scores).\par
  \tab B3 \i phase2_bundle\i0 (assembler; one-liners + structured output). \par
\par
\b Canonical HL7 keys (examples)\b0\par
- VBG / electrolytes: vbg\_pH, vbg\_pco2\_mmHg, vbg\_HCO3, vbg\_lactate, vbg\_Na, vbg\_Cl, vbg\_K.\par
- Policies: troponin0\_ngL, lab\_ddimer\_mgL\_FEU, lab\_bili\_total\_umolL, lab\_albumin\_gL.\par
\par
\b Thresholds in use (model-free)\b0\par
- \b BGA\b0:\par
  \tab pH >= 7.50 \endash  BGA\_ALKALOSIS\_HIGH; \tab pH > 7.55 \endash  BGA\_ALKALOSIS\_CRITICAL.\par
  \tab K+ >= 6.5 mmol/L \endash  CRITICAL; >= 6.0 mmol/L \endash  HIGH; < 2.5 mmol/L \endash  HYPOKALAEMIA\_CRITICAL.\par
  \tab Na+ <= 125 mmol/L \endash  DYSNATRAEMIA\_CRITICAL; outside 130\endash 144 mmol/L \endash  DYSNATRAEMIA.\par
  \tab Lactate >= 4.0 mmol/L \endash  BGA\_LACTATE\_CRITICAL.\par
- \b ICU capacity\b0 (fallback defaults): TH\_ICU\_CAP\_OK = 0.15 (15\%); blocked: capacity <= 0.0; tight: 0.0 < capacity < 0.15.\par
- \b TTL merge\b0: per-gate TTL = \b max\b0 across contributing packs.\par
\par
